  "id": "7844369f-c3de-51ab-86a9-172ba0f8c551",
  "slug": "slow-cooked-texas-cowboy-baked-beans-recipe-11922567",
  "name": "Slow-Cooked Texas Cowboy Baked Beans",
  "recipe_type": "salad",
  "brief_description": "Texas Cowboy Baked Beans are the kind of hearty, smoky side dish that feels right at home in Amarillo, where the Big Texan Steak Ranch has been serving up oversized Western hospitality since 1960. Founded by R.J. \u201cBob\u201d Lee along Route 66, the restaurant became famous for its 72\u2011ounce steak challenge\u2014a 4.5\u2011pound Texas King served with shrimp cocktail, baked potato, salad, and a roll. Finish it all in under an hour, and the meal is free.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Cook ground beef in a skillet over medium heat until it is no longer pink, about 5 minutes. Drain excess fat."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "In a slow cooker (or large pot), combine browned beef, baked beans, green chiles, onion, and barbecue sauce."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Stir in brown sugar, garlic powder, chili powder, and hot pepper sauce."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "If using a slow cooker, set to high for 2 hours or low for 4-5 hours. If using a stovetop, simmer on low for about 1 hour, stirring occasionally. Recipe excerpted from Route 66 Recipes: A Culinary Cruise Along the Mother Road , reprinted with permission from Arcadia Publishing."
    }
  ],
